{"sections": [
  {"key": "arc", "title": "The arc", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Revenue compounded at 6.4% a year from $38.5 billion in FY2016 to $67.6 billion in FY2025 [F1][F10][F201]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The path was cyclical rather than steady: a 20.4% jump in FY2018 to $54.7 billion [F3][D92], a 22.4% collapse in FY2020 to $41.7 billion [F5][D198], then a 12.8% rise in FY2023 to $67.1 billion [F8][D357]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The FY2020 decline came from lower sales volume driven by lower end-user demand and dealer inventory reductions across all three primary segments [P59]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "FY2023's gain was primarily favorable price realization and higher sales volume, with dealer inventory up about $2.1 billion during the year [P32]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "drivers", "title": "What drove growth", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "North America supplied the latest year's growth, contributing 3.4pp of the 4.3% increase on a 54.2% revenue share [D515][D463][D513]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "North America sales rose 6% on higher sales volume, mainly higher sales of equipment to end users, partly offset by unfavorable price realization [P12]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Power & Energy carried the segment story, contributing 5.2pp on 11.6% growth, while Construction Industries subtracted 0.6pp [D759][D758][D766]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Construction Industries' $395 million decline was primarily unfavorable price realization of $1.136 billion, partly offset by higher sales volume of $568 million [P8]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating costs grew 4.8pp faster than revenue in FY2025, at 9.1%, and operating income fell 14.7% against revenue growth of 4.3% [D489][D481][D464][D463]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "margins", "title": "Margins and costs", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "The FY2025 operating margin of 16.5% sat 2.2pp above the 14.3% window median but 3.7pp below the FY2024 high of 20.2% [F30][D1123][F29][D476]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Cost of revenue took 4.2pp off the margin, while R&D added 0.1pp and SG&A was flat [D490][D491][D492]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "The operating profit decline was primarily unfavorable manufacturing costs of $2.148 billion and unfavorable price realization of $817 million, with manufacturing costs largely reflecting higher tariffs [P9]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "In FY2025 net margin of 13.1% sat 3.4pp below the 16.5% operating margin, a gap the pack puts at 3.4pp [F50][F30][D1168]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "cash", "title": "Cash conversion", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Operating cash flow of $11.7 billion was 1.32x net income in FY2025, above the 1.16x window median, and free cash flow of $8.9 billion was 1.00x [F80][F40][D450][D1158][F100][D451]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Free cash flow margin of 13.2% was above the 11.9% window median but below the 16.8% FY2023 high [D447][D1129][D1128]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Capex rose 41.9% to $2.8 billion, 4.2% of revenue and 1.25x D&A, the highest ratio in the window [F90][D470][D446][D452]."},
    {"type": "cause", "text": "Machinery, Power & Energy operating cash flow rose to $12.278 billion primarily on lower working capital requirements and lower cash taxes paid [P4]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "balance_sheet", "title": "Balance sheet and capital allocation", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Net debt stood at $26.2 billion, or -38.8% of revenue, in FY2025, with cash of $10.0 billion and a 1.44x current ratio [D456][D457][F140][F180]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "That net-cash ratio ranked at the 67th percentile of three industrials peers against a -59.4% median [D1169][D1170]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "The pack's total debt omits long-term debt due within one year, which the filer reports at $7.1 billion in FY2025, so the net debt figure understates borrowings [R7][X180][D455]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Buybacks of $5.2 billion plus dividends of $2.7 billion equaled 89.0% of free cash flow, and the diluted share count fell 3.5% [X140][X150][D459][D483]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "red_flags", "title": "Red flags", "sentences": [
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Long-term debt due within one year is in no line of the pack across FY2016-FY2025, running $5.3 billion to $9.1 billion a year and $7.1 billion in FY2025 [R7][X180]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "Every net-debt and total-debt figure here is therefore a partial measure, and the leverage picture is worse than the table shows [R7][D456]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Net debt rose for a second year in FY2025, from $22.1 billion in FY2023 to $24.9 billion in FY2024 and $26.2 billion in FY2025 [R1][D350][D403][D456]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "Debt-funded capital return while operating profit falls is the pattern to watch, though the omitted current maturities make the level uncertain [R1][D464]."},
    {"type": "fact", "text": "Net income for FY2021-FY2025 in the table comes from the proxy's pay-versus-performance table, not the 10-K, differing by up to 0.06% [R3][F40][X20]."},
    {"type": "judgement", "text": "The gap is immaterial to margins and cash conversion, but the 10-K figure should be used where precision matters [R3][X20]."}
  ]},
  {"key": "watch", "title": "What to watch", "sentences": [
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether the FY2026 10-K shows operating margin recovering above the 14.3% window median or falling further from the 16.5% FY2025 level [D1123][F30]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether capex stays above the 1.25x D&A ratio of FY2025 or falls back toward the 0.92x of FY2024 [D452][D399]."},
    {"type": "comparison", "text": "Whether net debt, on the pack's basis, moves back below the $24.9 billion FY2024 level or extends past $26.2 billion [D403][D456]."}
  ]}
]}
